title: "drift-point: token-level divergence measurement for compressed model replays"
authors:
  - family-names: Dhinwa
    given-names: Kapil
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kapildhinwa2010-dev/Draft_ponit_harness"
abstract: "A small harness that measures at which generated token a rank-k linear delta replay of a language model first diverges from the original model. CPU-only, no training, bounded evaluation."
keywords:
  - language-models
  - compression
  - interpretability
  - evaluation
